{"authored" [{"question" "q-6832" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "For the parametric curve\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{sin}(\\frac{\\pi t}{2}),\\,\\,\\,y=\\operatorname{cos}(\\frac{\\pi t}{3}),\\,-3\\le t\\le 3,\n$$\n\nconsider the following table of values:\n\n| **$t$** | $-3$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $1$ | $0$ | $b$ | $0$ | $1$ | $0$ | $c$ |\n| $y$ | $a$ | $-\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $1$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $-\\frac{1}{2}$ | $-1$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nFind the value of $-a+b+c.$\n\nAnswer: {{answer}}" "category" "local_reconstruction" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/history-question-import-2026-10-04/import-ready/questions.json" "file_sha256" "50327f088e1802526fef61aecff55d85426669a0cf8ea00def90f5806b3d5934" "transaction" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/history-question-import-2026-10-04/import-ready/database-import/transaction.edn" "transaction_sha256" "735387c3560cc206e9e6dc540884b5be0d105253f5d3c2618709fce223388e6b" "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/history-question-import-2026-10-04/import-ready/database-import/verification.json" "basis" 552} {"question" "q-16149" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that a curve is defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx={t}^{2}+t,\\,\\,\\,y={t}^{2}-2,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\n$$\n\ndetermine the ranges of $x$ and $y.$\n\nX range: {{x-range}}\n\nY range: {{y-range}}" "category" "local_reconstruction" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/history-question-import-2026-10-04/import-ready/questions.json" "file_sha256" "50327f088e1802526fef61aecff55d85426669a0cf8ea00def90f5806b3d5934" "transaction" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/history-question-import-2026-10-04/import-ready/database-import/transaction.edn" "transaction_sha256" "735387c3560cc206e9e6dc540884b5be0d1