d curve:\n\n$$\nx=1-2t,\\,y=t,\\,-3\\le t\\le 3\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948638/state.json" "file_sha256" "d861e251665aa8f66e9fc750b615829a7af27a63204e9fbbe3201691e0a8edd4" "basis" 577 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948638/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-123783" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need to create a table of values and then sketch the curve. First, we work out the $x$-values using the formula $x=1-2t.$ This gives\n\n| **$t$** | $-3$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $7$ | $5$ | $3$ | $1$ | $-1$ | $-3$ | $-5$ |\n| $y$ | $$ | $$ | $$ | $$ | $$ | $$ | $$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nNow, we work out the $y$ values using $y=t.$ This gives\n\n| **$t$** | $-3$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $7$ | $5$ | $3$ | $1$ | $-1$ | $-3$ | $-5$ |\n| $y$ | $-3$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nPlotting these points, we obtain the following curve:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948638/assets/ef5f33b74b59b5a62fd8670a8feb6487b01a97aed4a44a098a576d10d891bd68.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948638/state.json" "file_sha256" "d861e251665aa8f66e9fc750b615829a7af27a63204e9fbbe3201691e0a8edd4" "basis" 577 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948638/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-123783" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948638/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e1117fbad5be03ecebc64ce9149e8