 "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948638/state.json" "file_sha256" "d861e251665aa8f66e9fc750b615829a7af27a63204e9fbbe3201691e0a8edd4" "basis" 577 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948638/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-16191" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Determine the graph of the following parametrically defined curve:\n\n$$\nx={t}^{2},\\,\\,\\,y=t(5-t),\\,0\\le t\\le 5\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13949104/state.json" "file_sha256" "355f4464dbf727c395f70ba753873f69c5911af145bebad590dda5b46fb69ac9" "basis" 561 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13949104/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-16191" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need to create a table of values and then sketch the curve. First, we work out the $x$-values using the formula $x={t}^{2}.$ This gives\n\n| **$t$** | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $4$ | $9$ | $16$ | $25$ |\n| $y$ | $$ | $$ | $$ | $$ | $$ | $$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nNow, we work out the $y$ values using $y=t(5-t).$ This gives\n\n| **$t$** | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $4$ | $9$ | $16$ | $25$ |\n| $y$ | $0$ | $4$ | $6$ | $6$ | $4$ | $0$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nPlotting these points, we obtain the following curve:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13949104/assets/1aa848f287660c0858d5d6478da71c5baab9252c13f0a2d4a48c38d61f6bce51.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13949104/state.json" "file_sha256" "355f4464dbf727c395f70ba753873f69c5911af145bebad590dda5b46fb69ac9" "basis"