on" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13949104/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-16191" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/image "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13949104/assets/64ac74a9f74475ad5ee699293d789221776f6764e525d1e057cfbaacdbb731b2.png"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13949104/state.json" "file_sha256" "355f4464dbf727c395f70ba753873f69c5911af145bebad590dda5b46fb69ac9" "basis" 561 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13949104/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-327880" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that a curve is defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +1,\\,y=-\\frac{7}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,0\\le \\theta <2\\pi ,\n$$\n\nwhat are the ranges of $x$ and $y?$\n\nThe range of $x$ is \n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}\n$x\\le $\n{{field-3}}.\n\nThe range of $y$ is \n{{field-4}}\n$\\le y$\n{{field-5}}{{field-6}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973156/state.json" "file_sha256" "6392d7caba96dda2d672f6d7393d4826a3a66a239df3843cec743f7a7a639adb" "basis" 668 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973156/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-327880" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's consider each variable in turn.\n\n- To find the range of $x,$ notice that for $0\\le \\theta <2\\pi ,$ \nwe have $-1\\le \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\le 1.$ Consequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & \\le \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\le 1 \\\\ -4 & \\le 4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\le 4 \\\\ -4+1 & \\le 4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +1\\le 4+1 \\\\ -3 & \\le x\\le 5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can conclude that $-3\\le x\\le 5.$\n\n- To find the range of $y,$ notice that for $0\\le \\theta <2\\pi ,$ \nwe have $-1\\le \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\le 1.$ Consequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & \\le \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\le 1 \\\\ \\frac{7}{2} & \\text{ }\\ge -\\frac{7}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\text{ }\\ge -\\frac{7}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{7}{2} & \\le -\\frac{7}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\le \\frac{7}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{7}{2} & \\le y\\le \\frac{7}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can conclude that $-\\frac{7}{2}\\le y\\le \\frac{7}{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973156/state.json" "file_sha256" "6392d7caba96dda2d672f6d7393d4826a3a66a239df3843cec743f7a7a639adb" "basis" 668 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973156/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-327880" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973156/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b831a1b72106ea95d4e79ccbaf8f78b64c9b28342b22f65be5511b4eb3a1a38d" "basis" 668 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973156/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-327880" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973156/state.json" "file_sha256" "6392d7caba96dda2d672f6d7393d4826a3a66a239df3843cec743f7a7a639adb" "basis" 668 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973156/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-327880" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-3"] "category" "ma_successful_gra