stion-capture/13973156/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-327880" "field" "field-6" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973156/state.json" "file_sha256" "6392d7caba96dda2d672f6d7393d4826a3a66a239df3843cec743f7a7a639adb" "basis" 668 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973156/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-327880" "field" "field-6" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{7}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973156/state.json" "file_sha256" "6392d7caba96dda2d672f6d7393d4826a3a66a239df3843cec743f7a7a639adb" "basis" 668 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973156/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-326251" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the curve with parametric equations\n\n$$\nx=\\sqrt{\\,t+4\\,},\\,y=\\frac{3}{2}{t}^{2}-t,\\,-3\\le t\\le 2.\n$$\n\nFill in the blanks in the following table of values:\n\n| **$t$** | $-3$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | {{field-1}} | $\\sqrt{2}$ | $\\sqrt{3}$ | $2$ | $\\sqrt{5}$ | $\\sqrt{6}$ |\n| $y$ | $\\frac{33}{2}$ | $8$ | {{field-2}} | $0$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | {{field-3}} |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038739/state.json" "file_sha256" "04ee7a68d2030797b5734e4b1aed9f05e0ee75f180ee5fd6ab516739b5a92b6b"} {"question" "q-326251" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "- To find the value of $x(-3),$ we substitute $t=-3$ into $x=\\sqrt{\\,t+4\\,}.$ This gives\n\n$$\nx(-3)=\\sqrt{-3+4}=\\sqrt{1}=1.\n$$\n\n- To find the value of $y(-1),$ we substitute $t=-1$ into $y=\\frac{3}{2}{t}^{2}-t.$ This gives\n\n$$\ny(-1)=\\frac{3}{2}(-1)^{2}-(-1)=\\frac{3}{2}+1=\\frac{3}{2}+\\frac{2}{2}=\\frac{5}{2}.\n$$\n\n- To find the value of $y(2),$ we substitute $t=2$ into $y=\\frac{3}{2}{t}^{2}-t.$ This gives\n\n$$\ny(2)=\\frac{3}{2}(2)^{2}-(2)=6-2=4.\n$$\n\nThen the table is \n\n \n\n| **$t$** | $-3$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $1$ | $\\sqrt{2}$ | $\\sqrt{3}$ | $2$ | $\\sqrt{5}$ | $\\sqrt{6}$ |\n| $y$ | $\\frac{33}{2}$ | $8$ | $\\frac{5}{2}$ | $0$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $4$ |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038739/state.json" "file_sha256" "04ee7a68d2030797b5734e4b1aed9f05e0ee75f180ee5fd6ab516739b5a92b6b"} {"question" "q-326251" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038739/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9042a3bb57b43217cf1bb0cf5cc16f1106958207637db566b7d3aa09aea4bef8"} {"question" "q-326251" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038739/state.json" "file_sha256" "04ee7a68d2030797b5734e4b1aed9f05e0ee75f180ee5fd6ab516739b5a92b6b"} {"question" "q-326251" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038739/state.json" "file_sha256" "04ee7a68d2030797b5734e4b1aed9f05e0ee75f180ee5fd6ab516739b5a92b6b"} {"question" "q-326251" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academ