find the value of $x(0),$ we substitute $t=0$ into $x=cos\\,(\\frac{\\pi t}{2}).$ This gives\n\n$$\nx(0)=cos\\,(\\frac{\\pi (0)}{2})=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)=1.\n$$\n\n- To find the value of $y(1),$ we substitute $t=1$ into $y=tan\\,(\\frac{\\pi t}{3}).$ This gives\n\n$$\ny(1)=tan\\,(\\frac{\\pi (1)}{3})=tan\\,(\\frac{\\pi }{3})=\\sqrt{3}.\n$$\n\n- To find the value of $x(2),$ we substitute $t=2$ into $x=cos\\,(\\frac{\\pi t}{2}).$ This gives\n\n$$\nx(2)=cos\\,(\\frac{\\pi (2)}{2})=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )=-1.\n$$\n\nThen the table is \n\n \n\n| **$t$** | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $0$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n| $y$ | $-\\sqrt{3}$ | $0$ | $\\sqrt{3}$ | $-\\sqrt{3}$ | $0$ | $\\sqrt{3}$ |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038739/state.json" "file_sha256" "04ee7a68d2030797b5734e4b1aed9f05e0ee75f180ee5fd6ab516739b5a92b6b"} {"question" "q-326256" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038739/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9042a3bb57b43217cf1bb0cf5cc16f1106958207637db566b7d3aa09aea4bef8"} {"question" "q-326256" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038739/state.json" "file_sha256" "04ee7a68d2030797b5734e4b1aed9f05e0ee75f180ee5fd6ab516739b5a92b6b"} {"question" "q-326256" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038739/state.json" "file_sha256" "04ee7a68d2030797b5734e4b1aed9f05e0ee75f180ee5fd6ab516739b