/state.json" "file_sha256" "04ee7a68d2030797b5734e4b1aed9f05e0ee75f180ee5fd6ab516739b5a92b6b"} {"question" "q-326242" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "- To find the value of $x(-1),$ we substitute $t=-1$ into $x=\\frac{3}{2}t+1.$ This gives\n\n$$\nx(-1)=\\frac{3}{2}(-1)+1=-\\frac{3}{2}+\\frac{2}{2}=-\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\n- To find the value of $y(-1),$ we substitute $t=-1$ into $y=-\\frac{5}{4}t+2.$ This gives\n\n$$\ny(-1)=-\\frac{5}{4}(-1)+2=\\frac{5}{4}+\\frac{8}{4}=\\frac{13}{4}.\n$$\n\n- To find the value of $x(3),$ we substitute $t=3$ into $x=\\frac{3}{2}t+1.$ This gives\n\n$$\nx(2)=\\frac{3}{2}(3)+1=\\frac{9}{2}+\\frac{2}{2}=\\frac{11}{2}.\n$$\n\nThen the table is \n\n \n\n| **$t$** | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $-\\frac{1}{2}$ | $1$ | $\\frac{5}{2}$ | $4$ | $\\frac{11}{2}$ | $7$ |\n| $y$ | $\\frac{13}{4}$ | $2$ | $\\frac{3}{4}$ | $-\\frac{1}{2}$ | $-\\frac{7}{4}$ | $-3$ |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038739/state.json" "file_sha256" "04ee7a68d2030797b5734e4b1aed9f05e0ee75f180ee5fd6ab516739b5a92b6b"} {"question" "q-326242" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038739/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9042a3bb57b43217cf1bb0cf5cc16f1106958207637db566b7d3aa09aea4bef8"} {"question" "q-326242" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038739/state.json" "file_sha256" "04ee7a68d2030797b5734e4b1aed9f05e0ee75f180ee5fd6ab516739b5a92b6b"} {"question" "q-326242" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{1}{2}"] "ca