6739b5a92b6b"} {"question" "q-16190" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need to create a table of values and then sketch the curve. First, we work out the $x$-values using the formula $x={t}^{2}-2.$ This gives\n\n| **$t$** | $-3$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $7$ | $2$ | $-1$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $2$ | $7$ |\n| $y$ | $$ | $$ | $$ | $$ | $$ | $$ | $$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nNow, we work out the $y$ values using $y=3-t.$ This gives\n\n| **$t$** | $-3$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $7$ | $2$ | $-1$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $2$ | $7$ |\n| $y$ | $6$ | $5$ | $4$ | $3$ | $2$ | $1$ | $0$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nPlotting these points, we obtain the following curve:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038739/assets/6a66ca74691344866c4f754edf36acc2f5301a0eeecee6340a0a701ad99f5fd6.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038739/state.json" "file_sha256" "04ee7a68d2030797b5734e4b1aed9f05e0ee75f180ee5fd6ab516739b5a92b6b"} {"question" "q-16190" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038739/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9042a3bb57b43217cf1bb0cf5cc16f1106958207637db566b7d3aa09aea4bef8"} {"question" "q-16190" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038739/state.json" "file_sha256" "04ee7a68d2030797b5734e4b1aed9f05e0ee75f180ee5fd6ab516739b5a92b6b"} {"question" "q-16190" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["image" "/home/jake/Developer